WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.698
A spreadsheet organises your data in a grid of rows and columns.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.862
Put headings in row one, like date, market, item and price.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.535
Use one row for each record: one sale, or one price check.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:19.188
Keep only numbers in number columns. Put the unit, like L R D, in the heading.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.356
And don't leave blank rows in the middle of your data.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:31.699
Before you move on, check: Create a sheet with headings in row 1. Enter five records, one per row. Keep only numbers in number columns.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.926
In the next lesson: Cleaning data.
